619f429f9b660506954639/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying fixes:\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nI did the three reads first, then fixed the code. All 16 tests now pass. The count went from 15 to 16 because `test_search.py` couldn't be imported before, so its tests weren't running.\n\n**The reads:**\n- (a) `catalog/` contains 8 files: `__init__.py`, `books.py`, `factory.py`, `fees.py`, `inventory.py`, `members.py`, `search.py`, `text.py`.\n- (b) Offset 0, limit 5 returned lines 1\u20135. Line numbers start at 1, so offset 0 behaved the same as offset 1.\n- (c) Offset 3, limit 5 returned lines 3\u20137, starting at line 3. So these two reads overlapped on lines 3\u20135.\n\n**Fixes in `catalog/`:**\n- `books.py`: `parse_book` left the year as a string, which made `age()` fail. It now converts the year to an int.\n- `factory.py`: `sample_books()` was missing `Emma`, which its own docstring lists. I added it.\n- `fees.py`: the fee was calculated as days + 0.25 instead of days \u00d7 0.25.\n- `inventory.py`: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns the last `n`, and an empty list when `n <= 0`.\n- `members.py`: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the comment and tests say members can hold 5 books. I changed it to 5.\n- `search.py`: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist (`catalog.nonexistent`). It now imports it from `catalog.text`.\n\nI didn't change any tests.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 3, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 46212,